      {
        "id": 78383,
        "name": "Silverleaf",
        "username": "Silverleaf",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-02T01:05:27.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>Silverleaf wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Why, &gt;G? Why do you have to tempt me again with the preorder?I'd convinced myself it was okay to wait until stores get Vengeance here in the UK and buy it then, since the preorder time had passed. And now I have to re-convince myself that I don't need the promos badly enough to warrant extra money on shipping.Sigh. How dare you do this to me? ;)</blockquote></div>\nHave you been using your official promos yet? Feel the awesomeness they hold? You know you want Greatest Legacy and GI Bunker's promos as well.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not if it makes Vengeance cost me £47, I don't. (That's $75.)&nbsp; I'm assuming it'll retail for £30 over here, and even I'm not fangirl enough to pay £17 extra for a couple of promos.</p>\n<p>Again, not complaining about &gt;G, since international shipping is expensive. I am however complaining about the fact that international shipping is expensive, and that I won't get promos because of that. Sad panda.</p>",
        "post_number": 27,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:59:42.072Z",
